📦 JAVA ARRAYS – ORAL CHEAT SHEET (DETAILED)
⭐ 1. ARRAYS (INTRODUCTION)
An array is a data structure in Java used to store multiple values of the same data type in a single variable.
👉 It stores elements in continuous memory locations.
⭐ 2. DECLARING ARRAYS
✔ Syntax:
Java
dataType[] arrayName;
✔ Example:
Java
int[] marks;
⭐ 3. CREATING ARRAYS
✔ Syntax:
Java
arrayName = new dataType[size];
✔ Example:
Java
marks = new int[5];
⭐ 4. DECLARATION + CREATION TOGETHER
Java
int[] marks = new int[5];
⭐ 5. INITIALIZING ARRAYS
Java
int[] marks = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};
⭐ 6. ACCESSING ARRAY ELEMENTS
Index starts from 0
Java
System.out.println(marks[0]);
⭐ 7. ARRAY EXAMPLE PROGRAM
Java
class ArrayDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] marks = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};

        for(int i = 0; i < marks.length; i++) {
            System.out.println(marks[i]);
        }
    }
}
⭐ 8. PASSING ARRAY TO METHOD
Arrays can be passed as arguments.
Java
class Test {
    void show(int[] arr) {
        for(int i : arr) {
            System.out.println(i);
        }
    }
}
⭐ 9. MULTIDIMENSIONAL ARRAYS
An array of arrays (matrix form).
✔ Syntax:
Java
int[][] matrix = new int[2][2];
✔ Example:
Java
class Matrix {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[][] a = {
            {1, 2},
            {3, 4}
        };

        System.out.println(a[0][1]);
    }
}
👉 Output: 2
⭐ 10. VARIABLE LENGTH ARGUMENTS (VARARGS)
Used when number of arguments is unknown.
✔ Syntax:
Java
void show(int... numbers)
✔ Example:
Java
class Test {
    void display(int... nums) {
        for(int n : nums) {
            System.out.println(n);
        }
    }
}
👉 Can pass:
Java
display(1,2,3);
display(10,20);
⭐ 11. COMMAND LINE ARGUMENTS
Arguments passed at runtime from command line.
✔ Example:
Java
class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(args[0]);
    }
}
👉 Run like:

java Test Hello
👉 Output:

Hello
🧾 ONE-LINE ORAL ANSWERS
✔ Array: Collection of same type elements
✔ Index: Position of element starting from 0
✔ Multidimensional array: Array of arrays
✔ Varargs: Method accepting variable number of arguments
✔ Command line arguments: Input given at runtime
✔ Passing array: Sending array as method parameter